    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0711" n="612" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg612"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/4097: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-12-14T18:00:00+00:00">December 14, 1936—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 14—2:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>610. Department’s 442, December 10, 6. p.m.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d559-f1"/> I
                    understand the press carries the substance of the four Governments’ replies to
                    the Franco-British <hi rendition="#italic">démarche</hi>. Foreign Office points
                    out all these replies support the work of the London Non-intervention Committee
                    but that Germany, Italy and Portugal offer no support for the principle of
                    mediation, the German Government in particular pointing out it has already
                    recognized the Franco regime.</p>
                <p>London Non-intervention Committee has already consulted both sides in Spain as to
                    more extended control of importation of arms but as yet has received no
                    reply.</p>
                <pb facs="0712" n="613" xml:id="pg613"/>
                <p>British and French Governments are conferring as to further possible steps which
                    might lead to successful mediation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
